# Go build artifacts
/bin/
/dist/
/bridge
*.exe
*.test
*.out

# Release artifact: written to repo root by goreleaser's before-hook
# so it doesn't trip the dist-must-be-empty check; uploaded as a
# Release asset via release.extra_files.
/release-meta.json

# Runtime state (local dev)
/bridge.db
/bridge.db-*
/data/
*.pem
*.key
*.crt

# Editor / OS
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp

# Claude Code local config
/.claude/

# Docker compose local overrides + the operator's env file. `.env` may hold
# secrets (TS_AUTHKEY, etc.) — never commit it. The `.env.example` template
# IS committed (the `!` re-includes it).
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
/compose.override.yaml
/compose.override.yml
/docker-compose.override.yaml
/docker-compose.override.yml

# Operator-local host coordinates (see ops/README.md) — never commit real
# WAN/LAN IPs, SSH targets, or key paths to this public repo.
ops/*.local.md

# Codebase audits. These enumerate weaknesses with file:line and fix sketches —
# an exploit index against every bridge whose operator hasn't upgraded yet.
# Moving them out of docs/ (PR #541) only stopped GitHub *Pages* from serving
# them; the repo is public, so tracked files stayed readable at
# raw.githubusercontent.com. Keep them local — see ops/README.md.
ops/*audit*.md
# Same reasoning for review findings: a bug-review / findings doc enumerates
# UNFIXED weaknesses, which is an exploit index for anything not yet shipped.
ops/*bug-review*.md
ops/*review*.md
ops/*findings*.md
